  "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
  "text": "\n \n                APPROVAL MEMORANDUM - No. 22 Chapter 566\n \n       MEMORANDUM filed with Senate Bill Number 6228-A, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT to authorize the commissioner of general services to trans-\n        fer and convey certain state land to the city of New Rochelle\"\n \n    APPROVED\n \n  This bill seeks to authorize the Office of General Services to  convey\nthe  state  land  located  at  Cedar  Street  Southbound  Extension, New\nRochelle, New York to the City of New Rochelle. The property  is  to  be\nused  exclusively  for  the  construction of municipal facilities and to\nsatisfy the affordable housing needs of residents of  the  City  of  New\nRochelle, and that upon termination of such use the property will revert\nback to the state.\n \n  While  I  support  the  provisions  of  the  bill, there are, however,\nseveral technical issues that must be clarified within the bill  regard-\ning the intended uses of the subject property. The Executive has secured\nan  agreement  with  the Legislature to pass legislation in the upcoming\nsession to address these concerns. On this  basis,  I  am  signing  this\nbill.\n \n  This bill is approved.                      (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                                ______\n",
  "year": 2019
